*Eigenstate Uncertainty:* The position and momentum uncertainties (standard deviations) for a state are defined as $sigma_x = sqrt(chevron.l x^2 chevron.r - chevron.l x chevron.r^2)$ and $sigma_p = sqrt(chevron.l p^2 chevron.r - chevron.l p chevron.r^2)$. For stationary number states $|n chevron.r$ of a harmonic oscillator, these can be evaluated using ladder operator expansions.
